>Amoghavarsha I</a> begins a 64-year reign and later founds <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manyakheta">Manyakheta</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 916</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indra-iii">Indra III</a> sacks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">949</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna-iii">Krishna III</a> defeats the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-takkolam">Battle of Takkolam</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">972</span><span class="rf-text">The Paramara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyaka">Siyaka II</a> sacks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manyakheta">Manyakheta</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">973</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tailapa-ii">Tailapa II</a> overthrows <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karka-ii">Karka II</a> and founds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a></span></li></ol>
